{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CghzvoxrxQJWyT7xBHuGW","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The ground state of high-spin octahedral Co²⁺ (d⁷) is ⁴T₁g(F). All three bands are measured from that level.\n\n**Method.** I built the full d⁷ ligand-field Hamiltonian over all 120 Slater determinants. It includes the d–d electron repulsion, written with the Racah parameters B and C, and the octahedral crystal field, written with Dq. I then diagonalised it. Each eigenvalue was labelled by its spin (from S²) and by its octahedral symmetry (from the C₄ character). I adjusted Dq, B and C until the three assigned levels matched the measured bands.\n\n**Result.** The fit reproduces all three bands exactly:\n\n| Level (above ⁴T₁g ground state) | Calculated (cm⁻¹) | Observed (cm⁻¹) |\n|---|---|---|\n| ⁴T₂g | 8 100 | 8 100 |\n| ⁴T₁g(P), counted as ⁴T₁(2) | 19 400 | 19 400 |\n| ²T₁g(2) | 21 600 | 21 600 |\n\nThere are three bands and three unknowns, so this is an exact solution rather than a least-squares fit. It gives no independent test of the model or the band assignments. The fit converged to the same answer from starting values of C = 3 000, 4 000 and 5 000 cm⁻¹.\n\nThe other levels predicted with these parameters:\n- ²E at about 9 900 cm⁻¹\n- ²T₁(1) at about 17 130 cm⁻¹\n- ⁴A₂g at about 17 300 cm⁻¹\n- ²T₂ at about 17 650 cm⁻¹\n\nThe ⁴A₂g level sits at 18Dq + 7.5B − ½√(…) ≈ 17 300 cm⁻¹, so the gap between it and ⁴T₂g, 10Dq = 9 215 cm⁻¹, is consistent with the fit.\n\n**Parameters:**\n- Dq ≈ 922 cm⁻¹, so 10Dq ≈ 9 220 cm⁻¹\n- B ≈ 828 cm⁻¹, about 85 % of the free-ion value of roughly 970 cm⁻¹\n- C ≈ 4 264 cm⁻¹, giving C/B ≈ 5.2\n\nThe quartet bands alone fix Dq and B. The spin-forbidden doublet band ²T₁(2) is what fixes C.\n\n{\"Dq\": 922, \"B\": 828, \"C\": 4264, \"out_of_scope\": false, \"reason\": \"Full d7 octahedral matrices reproduce all three assigned bands exactly with these parameters.\"}"}],"container"